<title>DUBAI: World's largest oil tanker due for Dubai repairs.</title>
<headline>World's largest oil tanker due for Dubai repairs.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 564,763 dwt ultra large crude carrier (ULCC) Jahre Viking will undergo general repair work next month in the Gulf Arab emirate of Dubai, Gulf shipping sources said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Jahre Viking, the world's largest oil tanker, will arrive at Dubai Dry Docks on November 5 for some three weeks of work, they added.</p>
<p>The Norwegian-flagged vessel is regularly fixed from the Saudi crude export terminal of Ras Tanura to the U.S. Gulf coast by major oil firms such as Exxon Corp.</p>
<p>-- Steven Swindells, Dubai Newsroom, +971 4 6071255</p>
</text>
